{"archetypes":[{"name":"harness-fidelity","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Verifies that the write_then_recover helper mirrors the actual SKILL.md Step 0b abort-before-recovery ordering with repo evidence, not just plan prose.","prompt_body":"Check whether the plan's claim that SKILL.md Step 0b issues exit 1 before the router-flag recovery block is actually borne out by the current SKILL.md text, and confirm that the proposed write_then_recover helper faithfully models that ordering with no elided intermediate steps. Look for any divergence between the plan's description of sub-step 6 and what SKILL.md actually says — including whether the recovery block is truly unreachable on writer failure or merely guarded by a conditional that could still execute on some code paths. Confirm that the helper's early-return-on-failure / spy-before-recovery-call structure maps 1-to-1 to the documented SKILL.md ordering so the test actually exercises the boundary it claims to exercise. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"schema-alignment","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Validates that the jq field names and argv flags used in Cases 7 and 7b match write-run-params.sh's actual emitted schema and accepted flags, preventing silent false-pass on name drift.","prompt_body":"Inspect the actual write-run-params.sh script to confirm that the field names in the Case 7b jq assertion (.manual_gate_b, .partition_requested, .brainstorm_requested) exist with exactly those names in the emitted JSON, since a renamed field causes jq -e to evaluate null which can silently pass a truthy-path assertion. Also verify that the --manual-gate-b and --classification argv flags accepted by write-run-params.sh match the names used in the write_then_recover helper, because a flag-name mismatch would make the writer exit non-zero for the wrong reason in Case 7 and produce a trivially passing test that does not actually prove the abort-before-recovery boundary. Check whether --classification BOGUS reliably exits non-zero before creating any output file, since the plan's no-file assertion in Case 7 depends on this pre-output abort. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
